---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profilePageSchema } from '../lib/schema';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About MD Anik Hasan | Builder and Founder of Boilabin"
  description="MD Anik Hasan is a CSE student and independent software builder in Dhaka, building Boilabin and learning difficult systems through practical work."
  schema={profilePageSchema()}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Builder profile"
    title="I learn difficult systems by making the parts real."
    intro="I’m MD Anik Hasan, a Computer Science and Engineering student at United International University and an independent builder in Dhaka. My main entrepreneurial focus is Boilabin."
    workshop="Builder Profile"
  />

  <div class="content-layout">
    <aside class="content-rail" aria-label="Profile summary">
      <div>
        <p class="rail-label">Based in</p>
        <p>Dhaka, Bangladesh</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="rail-label">Studying</p>
        <p>Computer Science and Engineering at UIU</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="rail-label">Available for</p>
        <p>Website and custom software development</p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <article class="prose">
      <h2>The work that connects everything</h2>
      <p>
        I like understanding a system from the inside, building it myself, and turning the result
        into a product that feels finished. That behavior appears in three different directions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Boilabin is the entrepreneurial direction. I am responsible for the product, platform
        experience, visual direction, systems, and launch preparation as its solo founder. It is
        pre-launch, so I keep private architecture and operations private instead of filling the
        gaps with public claims.
      </p>
      <p>
        Software is the practical engineering direction. SoctuKit is public proof of native Windows
        work. The UIU Discord Bot is proof of Python automation and integration for a real
        university community. I also take on website development where structure, interface quality,
        performance, and search foundations have to work together.
      </p>
      <p>
        Salty Potato AI is the learning direction: an experimental decoder-only language model,
        tokenizer, data pipeline, training process, checkpoint work, inference, and desktop
        software. I am building it to understand language models through implementation, not to
        claim a research title or compete with production systems.
      </p>

      <h2>How I choose tools</h2>
      <p>
        Python is where I currently have the strongest practical confidence. I have also worked with
        C, C++, Java, TypeScript, and the C#, .NET, WinUI 3, and XAML stack visible in SoctuKit.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do not want one framework to become my identity. The useful question is what the product
        needs, which tools are stable enough for it, and what I can verify at the end.
      </p>

      <h2>Working together</h2>
      <p>
        I can be hired for website development and custom software development. I am also open to
        useful open-source contributions and technical collaboration where I can learn and provide
        concrete work.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/hire/">Describe a paid project</a> or
        <a href="/open-source/">read the open-source boundary</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
